{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg6unF6FYKRDt1jTSFNUD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are 10 open-source vector databases. I wrote this from memory and didn't check the repos, so confirm licenses before relying on them, since projects sometimes relicense.\n\n| # | Database | GitHub URL | License | Language |\n|---|----------|-----------|---------|----------|\n| 1 | Milvus | https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus | Apache-2.0 | Go (with C++ core) |\n| 2 | Qdrant | https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant | Apache-2.0 | Rust |\n| 3 | Weaviate | https://github.com/weaviate/weaviate | BSD-3-Clause | Go |\n| 4 | Chroma | https://github.com/chroma-core/chroma | Apache-2.0 | Rust (core), Python and TypeScript clients |\n| 5 | pgvector | https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector | PostgreSQL License | C |\n| 6 | LanceDB | https://github.com/lancedb/lancedb | Apache-2.0 | Rust |\n| 7 | Vespa | https://github.com/vespa-engine/vespa | Apache-2.0 | Java and C++ |\n| 8 | Vald | https://github.com/vdaas/vald | Apache-2.0 | Go |\n| 9 | Marqo | https://github.com/marqo-ai/marqo | Apache-2.0 | Python |\n| 10 | txtai | https://github.com/neuml/txtai | Apache-2.0 | Python |\n\n- **pgvector** is a PostgreSQL extension, not a standalone database.\n- **Chroma** has a Rust core after its rewrite, but the project is still often described as Python.\n- **Faiss** (MIT, C++) is a similarity-search library rather than a database, so I left it out. If you want a stricter \"database only\" list, I'd also drop txtai, which is closer to an embeddings framework.\n- Good swap-ins are Elasticsearch/OpenSearch (vector search as a feature) and Typesense (GPL-3.0, C++).\n\nI can check each repo's current license and primary language if you'd like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6735,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"